<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="default">

    <!-- AXIS CONVENTION (kalıcı not - KURSAD_COMPETITION_AREA bloğunun DIŞINDA,
         generate_competition_area.py tarafından hiç dokunulmaz):
         Bu world'de Y ekseni = Kuzey = drone'un ileri (+N) ekseni; X ekseni
         = Doğu. px4-gz bridge PX4'ün local-NED north_m'sini bu world'ün Y
         eksenine eşliyor, X'e değil. Bu, 2026-08-13'te gerçek bir MAVSDK
         Offboard uçuşuyla ölçülüp kanıtlanmıştı (bir hedefin 15m KUZEYE değil
         15m DOĞUYA yerleştiği bir hatanın düzeltilmesi sırasında). Tam kanıt
         metni (ölçüm sonuçları dahil): generate_competition_area.py docstring'i,
         "BU KANITIN TAM METNİ" başlığı altında. -->

    <!-- Physics -->
    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.004</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>250</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <!-- Environment -->
    <gravity>0 0 -9.8</gravity>
    <magnetic_field>6e-06 2.3e-05 -4.2e-05</magnetic_field>
    <atmosphere type="adiabatic"/>

    <!-- Scene / lighting env -->
    <!--
      OUTDOOR LOOK, TIER 1 (2026-08-27). Scene level only: no geometry, no
      physics, no new bodies, no new lights, no textures, no Fuel includes.

      WHY: the arena read as a studio turntable (near white floor, flat
      neutral 0.7 backdrop) rather than an outdoor competition field.

      THE HARD CONSTRAINT that shapes every number below: the mission
      detects the blue hexagon, the red triangle and the coloured payload
      rectangles with ABSOLUTE HSV thresholds. There is no auto exposure
      and no white balance in the pipeline; CLAHE is applied to the V
      channel only. Live values, from the HSVContourDetector block of
      .scripts/olds/v34/v34_flight_stack/core/config/parameters.py
      (cited by NAME, not by line number, because that file moves):
        HSV_RED_LO_1  (0,40,40)    HSV_RED_HI_1  (15,255,255)
        HSV_RED_LO_2  (165,40,40)  HSV_RED_HI_2  (180,255,255)
        HSV_BLUE_LO   (90,80,40)   HSV_BLUE_HI   (140,255,255)
      So every surface added or recoloured in this world must be either
      near neutral (S below 30) or yellow green (H 35..80). Brown, ochre,
      terracotta, rust, dry grass and safety orange all land inside the
      RED mask (H 10..25 with S above 60) and are banned here.

      ambient 0.4 to 0.5. Lifts the inside of every cast shadow by 25%.
      The RED TRIANGLE is the tightest margin in the entire system: 1 m
      side is 0.433 m2, which projects to about 561 px2 at the 15 m
      mission altitude against HSV_MIN_AREA_TRI_BASE 390, a margin of
      only 1.44x. Anything that darkens or desaturates red, or drops a
      shadow across the triangle, is a mission risk. Shadow interiors
      therefore get BRIGHTER here, never darker.

      background 0.7 grey to 0.72 0.78 0.85. Pale sky haze instead of
      studio grey. OpenCV HSV of that colour, computed:
        R=0.72 G=0.78 B=0.85, max=B=0.85, min=R=0.72, delta=0.13
        V = 0.85*255                       = 217
        S = 255*0.13/0.85                  = 39
        H = 60*(4 + (R-G)/delta) = 212.3 deg, OpenCV H = 106
      H 106 IS inside the blue hue band [90,140], so the hue alone would
      not save it. The blue mask also demands S at or above 80, and this
      colour is S 39, less than half the floor. The horizon can therefore
      never register as blue even at the >40 deg vehicle tilts that put
      it in frame. It is out of the red mask on hue as well, since red is
      [0,15] u [165,180] and 106 is in neither.

      grid and shadows are unchanged.
    -->
    <scene>
      <grid>false</grid>
      <ambient>0.5 0.5 0.5 1</ambient>
      <background>0.72 0.78 0.85 1</background>
      <shadows>true</shadows>
    </scene>

    <!-- Ground plane -->
    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>1 1</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <surface>
            <friction>
              <ode/>
            </friction>
            <bounce/>
            <contact/>
          </surface>
        </collision>

        <!--
          OUTDOOR LOOK, TIER 1 (2026-08-27). VISUAL ONLY.

          THE <collision> BLOCK ABOVE IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. It is a
          <plane>, which DART treats as an INFINITE half space; its
          <size>1 1</size> is inert and does nothing. Every contact,
          landing and payload release test in this repo is calibrated
          against that half space, and tests/sdf_geometry.py parses this
          file for the payload mount poses. Changing the LOOK must not
          change the PHYSICS, so nothing outside this <visual> moves.

          0.8 near white to 0.30 0.30 0.31 mid grey asphalt. OpenCV HSV,
          computed:
            R=0.30 G=0.30 B=0.31, max=B=0.31, min=0.30, delta=0.01
            V = 0.31*255       = 79
            S = 255*0.01/0.31  = 8
            H = 60*(4 + (0.30-0.30)/0.01) = 240 deg, OpenCV H = 120
          S 8 is below BOTH mask saturation floors (red needs S at or
          above 40, blue needs S at or above 80), so this surface is
          unconditionally invisible to the detector however it is lit.
          It is also the biggest free win available for the red triangle:
          the old 0.8 floor was almost as bright as the targets, so red
          and blue sat on a low contrast field. A mid grey apron makes
          both markers pop, which helps the colour fraction gates
          (HSV_COLOR_FRAC_TRI_BASE 0.35, HSV_COLOR_FRAC_HEX 0.45) and
          gives CLAHE on V a much better histogram to work with.

          cast_shadows false. A 500 m plane is the largest caster in the
          world and it can only ever shadow itself, so switching it off
          changes nothing visible and drops it out of the PSSM shadow
          passes. This edit is a net performance SAVING.

          specular 0.8 to 0. Matte asphalt. A bright specular lobe on the
          ground beside a marker is exactly the sort of near white
          highlight that drags saturation down, and blue_hexagon is
          already deliberately glossy (its own material carries specular
          0.9 0.9 0.9 1).
        -->
        <visual name="visual">
          <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>500 500</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.30 0.30 0.31 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.30 0.30 0.31 1</diffuse>
            <specular>0 0 0 0</specular>
          </material>
        </visual>

        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>

        <inertial>
          <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
          <mass>1</mass>
          <inertia>
            <ixx>1</ixx>
            <ixy>0</ixy>
            <ixz>0</ixz>
            <iyy>1</iyy>
            <iyz>0</iyz>
            <izz>1</izz>
          </inertia>
        </inertial>

        <enable_wind>false</enable_wind>
      </link>

      <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <self_collide>false</self_collide>
    </model>

    <!--
      YARISMA ALANI (2026-08-30, tek parkur mimarisi).

      Onceki iki lane duzeni (Lane A merkez X=0 ve Lane B merkez X=50)
      kaldirildi. Artik TEK bir 30 m (X) x 100 m (Y) parkur var ve dort
      hedefin dordu birden onun icinde: Mavi Altigen, Kirmizi Ucgen,
      Kirmizi Kare, Mavi Kare. Parkur merkezi X=0, Y araligi [0, 100].

      Arac spawn'i safe_sitl_launcher.sh'te set edilir:
      PX4_GZ_MODEL_POSE="0,-25,0,0,0,1.5707963". Parkurun X merkezine
      ortalanmis, guney ucundan 25 m disarida, yaw = pi/2 ile parkura
      (+Y = Kuzey) bakar. Degisken kaldirilirsa Gazebo kendi
      varsayilanina (orijin, yaw 0) doner.

      EKSEN KURALI: "ileri" = +Y = Kuzey; +X = Dogu. Tam MAVSDK ucus
      kaniti icin generate_competition_area.py docstring'ine bakin
      (2026-08-13: north=15 komutu araci dunya (0,15)'e goturdu, east=15
      ise (15,0)'daki propun tam ustune indirdi, yani px4 gz bridge NED
      north_m'yi bu world'un Y eksenine esliyor, X'e degil).

      SEKILLERIN KONUMU ELLE DUZENLENMEZ. Asagidaki dort include,
      generate_competition_area.py tarafindan HER SITL acilisinda
      (safe_sitl_launcher.sh adim 4a) yeniden uretilir. Marker'lar
      ARASINDAKI her sey ustune yazilir; disindaki hicbir sey degismez.
      Buradaki degerler yalnizca ilk acilisa kadar gecerli baslangic
      degerleridir (kisitlari saglarlar).
    -->

    <!-- Parkur siniri: 30 x 100 m notr gri cerceve, GORSEL SADECE
         (collision yok, fizik govdesi yok, HSV tespitine gorunmez).
         Alan merkezine yerlestirilir: X=0, Y=50, yani Y araligi [0, 100].
         generate_competition_area.py bu include'a DOKUNMAZ. -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://competition_boundary</uri>
      <name>competition_boundary</name>
      <pose>0 50 0 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>

    <!-- KURSAD_COMPETITION_AREA_START -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://blue_hexagon</uri>
      <name>blue_hexagon</name>
      <pose>-7.408 51.413 0.003 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>

    <include>
      <uri>model://red_triangle</uri>
      <name>red_triangle</name>
      <pose>10.944 18.728 0.003 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>

    <include>
      <uri>model://red_square</uri>
      <name>red_square</name>
      <pose>10.263 42.742 0.003 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>

    <include>
      <uri>model://blue_square</uri>
      <name>blue_square</name>
      <pose>10.503 35.215 0.003 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>
    <!-- KURSAD_COMPETITION_AREA_END -->



    <!-- ADR-011: RED-servo (Mavi Altigen target) payload. Exists from world load and is held to the
         x500 by a DetachableJoint (see the vehicle model). Mounted RIGHT (-y).

         F2 (2026-08-17) MOVED THIS OUTBOARD, 0.20 -> 0.28 m, and down to
         its exact resting height. The original 0.20 m put the payload's
         volume (z [0.000,0.050], |y| [0.0875,0.3125]) straight through the
         landing skid (z [0.0136,0.0286], |y| [0.1245,0.1395]). Nothing
         pushed them apart while the DetachableJoint held, because DART
         suppresses collision between joint-connected bodies, but the
         instant the joint was removed the solver saw a deeply
         interpenetrating pair and EJECTED the payload. That, not the
         detach message, is what threw payload 2 to 4.9 m off the triangle
         and left payload 1 standing on its edge. Clearance now needs
         |y| >= 0.1395 + 0.1125 = 0.252; 0.28 leaves 2.8 cm.
         z 0.06 -> 0.025 so the body starts exactly at rest on the ground
         instead of dropping 3.5 cm while the joint is forming.
         COST, recorded honestly: a side-mounted payload lands where its
         MOUNT is, so centring the camera on the target now leaves a
         systematic 0.28 m miss (was 0.20 m). See ADR-011.
         Colour is TRUE RED (operator requirement, 2026-08-17 F1): the real
         payload is red, and a stand-in hue would make every colour-based
         observation in the sim untransferable. It therefore sits squarely
         inside the detector's red mask (hue 0, S 238, V 191 vs the
         [0,15]u[165,180] S>=40 V>=40 band) and separation from the arena
         targets comes from SIZE, not colour: at the 15 m mission altitude
         a 0.30x0.225 m prism projects to 10.8x8.1 px = 87 px2, against
         HSV_MIN_AREA_TRI_BASE 390 and HSV_MIN_AREA_RECT_BASE 400, a 4.5x
         margin. The gate is only reached below ~7 m altitude.
         Cross-colour mapping helps too: this RED payload is dropped on the
         BLUE hexagon, so a released payload never lies on a same-colour
         target.
         Mass 0.15 kg in simulation, NOT the real 1.05 kg: the sim x500 is a
         2.07 kg airframe, and two real payloads (+2.1 kg, +101%) would push
         thrust-to-weight and MPC_THR_HOVER far outside the tuning this SITL
         model ships with. Real value is recorded in real_system.yaml. -->
        <!--
      GERCEGE UYGUN OLCU/YERLESIM (operator, 2026-08-21). Onceki 0.30 x 0.225
      x 0.05 m govde ve -+0.28 m yan montaj gercek dusenegi yansitmiyordu.
      Yeni: uzun kenar 0.14, kisa kenar 0.05, yukseklik 0.07; iki yuk
      DRONE'UN TAM ALTINDA, uzun kenarlari gövde X'ine paralel, aralarinda
      2 cm bosluk -> merkezler y = -+0.035 (0.025 yarim genislik + 0.010
      yarim bosluk). Yerde dururken merkez z = 0.035 (yukseklik/2).

      Iniş takimi ile catisma yok: skid |y| araligi [0.1245, 0.1395], yukler
      |y| <= 0.06 - tamamen ice dusuyor, yani dunya SDF'sinin F2 notundaki
      "eklem cozulunce DART ic ice gecmis cifti gorup payload'i firlatiyor"
      tuzagina girmiyoruz.

      YAN FAYDA: yuk artik montaj noktasinda degil neredeyse govde
      merkezinde, yani "kamera hedefi ortaliyor ama yuk montaj noktasina
      dusuyor" sistematik hatasi 0.28 m'den ~0.035 m'ye iniyor.
    -->
    <model name="payload_red">
      <pose>0.035000 -25.000000 0.035 0 0 1.5707963268</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <inertial>
          <mass>0.15</mass>
          <inertia>
            <ixx>9.25e-5</ixx><iyy>3.06e-4</iyy><izz>2.76e-4</izz>
            <ixy>0</ixy><ixz>0</ixz><iyz>0</iyz>
          </inertia>
        </inertial>
        <!-- YUVA (BORE) COLLISION.
             Buradaki bloklar generate_bore_collision.py tarafindan URETILIR;
             marker'lar arasini elle duzenlemeyin. Profil (cep O46.50, pah-1
             23.20 derece, pah-2 46.97 derece, gecis deligi O22.00) ve faset
             sayisi N o script'te tek yerde tanimli.

             ONCEKI HALI tek bir kutuydu: <box><size>0.14 0.05 0.07</size></box>.
             O kutunun ust yuzeyi deck seviyesinde DUZ ve KAPALI oldugu icin
             kanca burnu yuvaya giremiyor, kapagin ustunde duruyordu; yanal
             kacisi engelleyen hicbir fiziksel sinir yoktu. Geometri zaten
             payload_body.stl icinde VARDI ve VISUAL olarak kullaniliyordu,
             yalnizca collision tarafinda atiliyordu. Uydurulmus bir sey
             eklenmedi; var olan yuzeyler tasindi. -->
        <!-- KURSAD_BORE_COLLISION_START -->
        <!-- URETILMIS BLOK -- generate_bore_collision.py yazar.
             ELLE DUZENLEME. Profil ve N o script'te tek yerde.
             Faset N=12, deck serit K=8, 83 kutu.
             CAD yuva: cep O46.50 (10.5mm derin), pah-1 23.20deg,
             pah-2 46.97deg, gecis deligi O22.00.
             Burun (O26, r 13.00) link z +19.14'de durur
             -> maks. girme 15.86 mm. Yanal sinir 10.25 mm. -->
        <collision name="bore_base">
          <pose>0.000000 0.000000 -0.009000 0.000000000 0.000000000 0.000000000</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.140000 0.050000 0.052000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <collision name="bore_fill_wall_00">
          <pose>-0.047100 0.012500 0.029750 0.000000000 0.000000000 0.000000000</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.045800 0.025000 0.010500</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <collision name="bore_fill_wall_01">
